## Cost & Licensing

- **Microsoft 365 Business Basic, Standard, and Premium mailboxes now support up to 100 GB of primary storage**, up from 50 GB, at no additional charge. Organizations that have been purchasing supplemental storage licenses or archiving solutions to work around the 50 GB cap should review whether those costs are still justified.

- **Digital signage on Teams panels requires Teams Rooms Pro or a Shared Space license.** Organizations considering the new idle-screen signage feature should confirm that their meeting room licenses qualify before investing in content or configuration work.

- **Windows 365 Flex and Cloud Apps are distinct licensing tiers.** The new Cloud Apps capability, which publishes individual Windows applications from a shared Cloud PC pool rather than providing each user a dedicated Cloud PC, may represent a lower-cost option for task-worker or occasional-use scenarios. Finance and IT leaders evaluating Windows 365 expansion should request a Flex versus dedicated Cloud PC cost comparison from their Microsoft account team.

*Sources: [Exchange Team Blog - 100 GB Mailbox](https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/t5/exchange-team-blog/understanding-the-new-100-gb-mailbox-entitlement-for-microsoft/ba-p/4548243) · [M365 Roadmap - Teams Panels Digital Signage](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=558852) · [Microsoft Mechanics - Windows 365](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MK-hCq7Su1w)*

