## Planning Horizon

**Immediate (this week):**

- **Immediate - [MacSync Stealer on macOS](https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/08/18/hunting-macsync-stealer-infrastructure-through-behavioral-pivots/):** Direct security operations to validate that Mac endpoints are covered by endpoint detection and response tooling and that conditional access policies require compliant device state before granting access to corporate resources.

**Within 30 days:**

- **Within 30 days - [Exchange Web Services retirement begins October 2026](https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/t5/exchange-team-blog/help-us-shape-exchange-server-on-premises-to-different-online/ba-p/4549691):** Commission an inventory of all applications, scripts, and integrations that use EWS, then prioritize remediation before October to avoid service interruptions.

- **Within 30 days - [Entra custom sign-in CSS retirement - October 26](https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/t5/microsoft-entra-blog/microsoft-entra-id-enhances-security-of-branded-sign-ins/ba-p/4537471):** Assign ownership of the sign-in page redesign to IT or brand teams so the work is complete before the October 26 deadline.

- **Within 30 days - [Outlook DLP for Mac and mobile - September GA](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=569719):** Compliance and IT teams should validate that existing DLP policies are correctly scoped to cover Mac and mobile users when the feature launches, and draft employee communications for the wait-on-send experience.

- **Within 30 days - [Purview DLP for Calendar Events on mobile - September GA](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=569716):** Review whether meeting-invite content in your organization carries regulated data, and confirm that mobile device management enrollment is sufficient to enforce DLP policy on iOS and Android.

- **Within 30 days - [Purview Retention for Copilot Memory - September GA](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=569612):** Records management and legal teams should determine whether Copilot memory items fall within existing retention schedules or require a new policy before the feature reaches general availability.

**Within 60-90 days:**

- **Within 60-90 days - [Purview Data Security Investigations from endpoint DLP alerts - September GA](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=558547):** Update incident-response runbooks to incorporate the new investigation workflow, and confirm that the security operations team has the Purview permissions needed to use it.

- **Within 60-90 days - [Planner Capacity View - October GA](https://www.microsoft.com/microsoft-365/roadmap?id=569733):** Brief project managers and team leads on the upcoming capacity timeline view so they can plan to use it for Q4 resourcing decisions.

**Longer range (before April 2027):**

- **Before April 2027 - [Exchange Web Services full shutdown](https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/t5/exchange-team-blog/help-us-shape-exchange-server-on-premises-to-different-online/ba-p/4549691):** All EWS-dependent integrations must be migrated or replaced before Microsoft fully disables the protocol; procurement and vendor management should be engaged now for any third-party tools requiring vendor updates or contract changes.

