## If You Take No Action

**MacSync Stealer on unmanaged Mac endpoints:** Employees using macOS devices that are not enrolled in endpoint management or covered by endpoint detection tools are exposed to an active credential-harvesting campaign today. A successful attack can yield browser-stored passwords and session cookies that allow an attacker to authenticate as that employee, bypass multi-factor authentication, and move through corporate systems. For organizations subject to HIPAA, SOC 2, or cyber insurance requirements, an account takeover originating from an unmanaged endpoint is likely a reportable incident and a policy-compliance failure.

**Exchange Web Services retirement without an integration inventory:** Organizations that do not audit their EWS-dependent tools before October 2026 will experience unexplained failures as phased disablement begins. Calendar sharing, Free/Busy lookups, and any line-of-business application built on EWS will degrade or stop working entirely by April 2027. Remediation under time pressure is significantly more expensive than planned migration, and some vendor updates may require contract cycles that take months.

**Outlook DLP gap on Mac and mobile left unaddressed through September:** Until the September DLP features are live and correctly configured, Mac and mobile users can send emails and calendar invites containing regulated data without triggering any policy check. For covered entities under HIPAA or organizations bound by GDPR, this represents a period of documented non-enforcement that auditors and insurers may treat unfavorably if a data incident occurs in the interim.

